    "intro_html":  "Nachos are usually a plate you build to order and eat standing up. Baked as a sheet pan instead, they portion by weight and reheat without turning into a soggy mess, which is the whole trick. Tortilla chips under seasoned turkey, black beans, tomatoes and jalapenos, buried in cheese and finished with cilantro, sour cream and salsa. Each serving runs {{cal}} calories with \u003cstrong\u003e{{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}}\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
